<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Åland</h1><p class="st-meta">1921 CE – present · capital Mariehamn</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Demilitarised, Swedish-speaking island autonomy within Finland, created by a League of Nations decision in 1921 and still self-governing today.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Åland Islands, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a>, passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> in 1809 and were demilitarised after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a> in 1856. When Finland became independent, most Ålanders, who speak Swedish, wanted to join Sweden. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> ruled in 1921 that the islands belonged to Finland, but with guaranteed autonomy and protection of the Swedish language.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Åland governs itself through its own parliament, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parliament-of-aland">Lagting</a>, first convened in 1922 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-sundblom">Julius Sundblom</a>, and a government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariehamn">Mariehamn</a>, with powers over education, culture, policing and local economy. Swedish is the only official language, and the right of domicile restricts land ownership to residents. The islands remain demilitarised and neutral, and their economy rests on shipping, ferries and tourism.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Autonomy has been widened by later acts, and Åland gained its own flag in 1954 and its own stamps in 1984. When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a> joined the EU in 1995, Åland kept a special status outside the EU tax area. It remains an autonomous region of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/aland.jpg" alt="Åland" width="320" height="209"><figcaption>Image: created by Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_%C3%85land.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1921 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mariehamn</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Julius Sundblom</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swedish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Finland</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Åland Islands, Ahvenanmaa</dd></dl></aside></div>

